WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.033
China's 2015 crash began with a vertical climb.

2
00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:10.553
The Shanghai Composite rose roughly one hundred and fifty percent into June.

3
00:00:10.553 --> 00:00:12.698
Easy money was the story.

4
00:00:12.698 --> 00:00:15.015
Borrowed cash was the fuel.

5
00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.718
Borrowing magnifies a gain.

6
00:00:17.718 --> 00:00:23.105
But it leaves the investor's own money as a thin layer underneath.

7
00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:26.614
When prices slip, collateral shrinks first.

8
00:00:26.614 --> 00:00:30.205
Cross the threshold, and positions are sold.

9
00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:32.346
Now the loop closes.

10
00:00:32.346 --> 00:00:34.971
Forced sales hit the order book.

11
00:00:34.971 --> 00:00:41.206
Prices fall, more accounts breach limits, and more shares meet thinner bids.

12
00:00:41.206 --> 00:00:44.406
Selling does not just reflect the fall.

13
00:00:44.406 --> 00:00:46.375
It creates the next one.

14
00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:50.829
Authorities added liquidity and state-backed buying.

15
00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:52.807
That can slow the machine.

16
00:00:52.807 --> 00:00:56.305
But it cannot instantly create willing buyers.

17
00:00:56.305 --> 00:00:59.575
Leverage makes confidence the scarce asset.

18
00:00:59.575 --> 00:01:03.225
When it breaks, the feedback loop does the rest.
